    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361">

                <pb facs="0351" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/3439: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-04T19:00:00-04:00">November 4, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1091. With reference to the proposal of the Cuban Government to send a group to
                    Washington to discuss the 1943 crop, you are authorized to inform the Cuban
                    Government that this Government will be prepared to initiate the conversations
                    about November 12 or any time thereafter when it may be convenient for the Cuban
                    officials to arrive.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d361-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please notify the Department as soon as possible of the composition of the group
                    and their expected date of arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d361-f1" n="28" xml:id="d361-f1-content">
                <p>The conversations were begun in Washington on November 23 and continued through
                    December; thereafter negotiations were continued in Cuba.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
